<title>SWITZERLAND: Swissair 1996 load factor down to 69.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Swissair 1996 load factor down to 69.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swissair Schweizerische Luftverkehr AG said its load factor eased to 69.2 percent in 1996 from 69.4 percent in 1995 last year. Swissair gave following details:</p>
<p>				    Jan-Dec 1996  vs   Jan-Dec 1995</p>
<p> Total load factor		 69.2 pct   vs   69.4 pct</p>
<p> Passenger load factor	   64.6 pct   vs   64.4 pct</p>
<p> Passengers carried	     8,825,794   vs   8,627,496</p>
<p>A Swissair statement also gave following details in thousands of tonnes kilometres (tkm):</p>
<p> Available tkm		   5,544,284    vs   5,065,115</p>
<p> Total revenue tkm	     3,836,600    vs   3,513,142</p>
<p> Passenger revenue tkm	 2,149,968    vs   1,952,709</p>
<p> Mail/Cargo revenue tkm	1,686,632    vs   1,560,433</p>
<p>Swissair also published traffic figures for December, 1996</p>
<p>					 Dec 1996   vs   Dec 1995</p>
<p> Total load factor		 68.4 pct   vs   68.3 pct</p>
<p> Passenger load factor	   61.2 pct   vs   60.9 pct</p>
<p> Passengers carried		 687,438   vs   637,268</p>
<p>In tousands of tonnes kilometres:</p>
<p> Available tkm:		    459,296    vs   414,968</p>
<p> Total revenue tkm		 314,218    vs   283,544</p>
<p> Passenger revenue tkm	   167,122    vs   150,791</p>
<p> Mail/Cargo revenue tkm	  147,096    vs   132,753</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
